e people elected next.", "author": "libsaremental", "created": 1792334921562, "profile_picture": "B8qfoXQAiSvx", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "stealthboy", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "The 3 Virginia proposed constitutional amendments on the November ballot.  Vote NO on all three and the reasons explained briefly...\n", "last_comment_created": 1792340395954, "content": "<p>Democrats have written confusing language into these constitutional amendment proposals so this is my attempt to clarify what they really mean.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Healthcare for women.  Vote NO.  Voting yes will give your minor children the right to make healthcare decisions, such as abortion, on their own WITHOUT parental consent or parents even being informed.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Marriage.  Voting yes changes the traditional marriage definition.  Vote NO and leave marriage as it should be, between a man and woman.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Voting.  Voting yes allows felons to vote.  Vote NO.  Give Democrats an inch and they'll take much more than a mile.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Liberals want all these amended to the Virginia constitution so that the law can't just be changed with the people elected next.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 2, "score_up": 35, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2111865563853066278", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATVjamJhY", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 21, "suggested_s